{"title":"2013 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The standard abbreviation for the non-terminating repeating decimal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/3/873b552312094e10e0a3205a9aa9a579d6c3cfac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$.34121121121121121\\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"182\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/0/c10f39837c58b3e4f3405e9af6a8c3cf1f7af3c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$.34\\overline{121}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />, a string of five digits. How many distinct non-terminating repeating decimals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/f/adf6067e29b6411188192720cd2320ab75c1c26f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$.d_1d_2d_3\\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"17\" /> have standard abbreviations that have at most six digits? (Consider two nonterminating decimals distinct if they differ in any digit. Nonterminating means that the digits are not eventually all zero.)\nCOMMENTS The standard abbreviation is also the shortest. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/8/d28bc2db27923ad2b34a3c5104794593643a7458.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$.34121121121121121\\ldots= .34\\overline{121}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"258\" height=\"15\" /> can also be abbreviated as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/5/2f5772c682509f6fe64e06416cdad4af3f32c215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$.341\\overline{211}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"59\" height=\"15\" />, or as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ecd93e9efc9c3fba88b201df86c26819e904165.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$.3412\\overline{112}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"68\" height=\"15\" />, or as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/0/7204b1e295dc2e1fe8d951b73fa58c90a86919b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$.34121\\overline{121}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" /> by sliding the bar rightward, making longer strings. The nonterminating decimal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/0/c10f39837c58b3e4f3405e9af6a8c3cf1f7af3c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$.34\\overline{121}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" /> has two parts: a repeating tail <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/5/7f5d1b02945a3eb6a7e3f83a140cb2a868481bfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T = \\overline{121}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"65\" height=\"15\" /> and a non-repeating head\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/4/8d4475304752a598d64dc09cf0c830901def41a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H = 34$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />. If the string has no head, the decimal is periodic, which is acceptable. There must be a tail string\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, which by convention is NOT permitted to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/6/59609a643a40ba21bbfd1f5ccb321fd2ce072a81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T = \\overline{0}$\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" />, since that corresponds to a terminating decimal. The examples <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/1/2c10f1a918e3c2dbefdead8feb17e83099d6cc6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$.\\overline{345}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/1/5c19f77915af177462a61bd4a38dce9d0bcd920a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$.\\overline{9}$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/d/d4dcb187ce2f137920d1c26ba5ae3c7bb6cf6ef1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$.721\\overline{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" /> are all standard abbreviations for nonterminating repeating decimals.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<pre><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/d/83d7907f9479118fe7af79711f6351d099cb1c4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5,778,810$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" />\n</pre>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_UNCO_Math_Contest_II\" title=\"2013 UNCO Math Contest II\">2013 UNCO Math Contest II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems\" title=\"2013 UNCO Math Contest II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2013 UNCO Math Contest II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://uncmathcontest.wordpress.com/\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\